<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 10, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">Every page written for animal service businesses now shares a link preview that speaks to them and points breeders to their own page. Before this, a shared provider link showed the site-wide image ("Professional breeding program management"), and breeders who followed the link had no way to find the breeder waitlist from a provider page.</p>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">What changed</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1">
    <li>New <code>ProviderLayout</code> wraps the base layout. <a href="/for-providers" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/for-providers</a>, every page under /for-providers and <a href="/list-your-facility" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/list-your-facility</a> use it. Page copy is unchanged.</li>
    <li>Link preview image for those pages is now <code>/og/providers.jpg</code>: "For Groomers, Trainers, Vets, Farriers, Boarding &amp; Other Animal Service Businesses" with "List your business free on the BreederHQ Marketplace". Titles and descriptions are unchanged.</li>
    <li>A strip above each page reads "Breeding animals? These pages are for service businesses." with a link to the breeder waitlist at <a href="/pricing#apply" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing#apply</a>.</li>
    <li>The /for-breeders title tag now ends "Records to Marketplace" in place of the herd-based wording, so it reads the same for every species.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">Not changed</h3>
  <p class="text-gray-700">The consumer-facing directory pages (/services/*, /dog-parks/*) and the comparison pages keep the default layout and image.</p>
</article>
